Description: rule-based proxy client with a built-in kernel
 Clash Qt is a Qt6 desktop client with its own C++ proxy kernel compiled
 into the process (no external core binary).
 .
 It supports rule-based routing (domain / IP-CIDR / GEOSITE / RULE-SET),
 VLESS (including REALITY), Hysteria2, HTTP and SOCKS5 inbounds, a fake-IP
 DNS server, connection tracking, and a TUN mode for transparent proxying
 of applications that ignore the system proxy settings.
